// @probe reject: `registry_search` is gone
// It answered from twelve package names compiled into the runtime. None exist, no index was ever
// queried, and there is no Varg registry to query — so every caller got a plausible list of
// things it could not install. `vargc search` and `vargc install` told the same story from the
// command line, and `install` downloaded without reading the checksum field it carried.
agent Main {
    public void Run() {
        var found = registry_search("http");
        print found.len();
    }
}
